-- title:
--   Vélu's double full-kernel quotient is multiplication by N
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, $N$ a positive integer with $N \neq 0$ in $K$, and $W$ an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $K$. For a point $Q$ of the affine curve $W$ write $W' =$ `W.fullKernelQuotient Q N` for the Weierstrass curve with the same $a_1, a_2, a_3$ and with $a_4$ and $a_6$ replaced by $a_4 - 5t$ and $a_6 - b_2 t - 7w$, where $t = \sum (3x^2 + 2a_2x + a_4 - a_1y)$ and $w = \sum \bigl(x(3x^2+2a_2x+a_4-a_1y) + y(2y+a_1x+a_3)\bigr)$, the sums being taken over the finite set of coordinate pairs $(x,y)$ of the points $k \cdot Q$ for $k \in [1, N-1]$ (the point at infinity contributing $(0,0)$). Assume: $Q$ has additive order exactly $N$; the discriminant of $W'$ is nonzero; $\varphi : W(K) \to W'(K)$ is an additive homomorphism with kernel the cyclic group generated by $Q$ whose coordinates at every $P \notin \langle Q \rangle$ are given by Vélu's sums $x(P) + \sum_{k=1}^{N-1}\bigl(x(P + kQ) - x(kQ)\bigr)$ and $y(P) + \sum_{k=1}^{N-1}\bigl(y(P + kQ) - y(kQ)\bigr)$; $Q'$ is a point of $W'$ of additive order exactly $N$ such that $\varphi(P) \in \langle Q' \rangle$ for every $P$ with $N \cdot P = 0$; the discriminant of $W'' =$ `(W.fullKernelQuotient Q N).fullKernelQuotient Q' N` is nonzero; and $\varphi' : W'(K) \to W''(K)$ is an additive homomorphism with kernel $\langle Q' \rangle$ given outside $\langle Q' \rangle$ by the same sum formulae relative to the multiples of $Q'$. Then there exist a Weierstrass variable change $C$ over $K$ and a proof $hC$ that $C \cdot W = W''$ such that the induced bijection $W''(K) \to W(K)$, `Point.equivOfVariableChangeEq hC`, carries $\varphi'(\varphi(P))$ to $N \cdot P$ for every point $P$ of $W$.
--
--   This is the statement that the full-kernel Vélu quotient of $W'=W/\langle Q\rangle$ by the image of the $N$-torsion returns, up to a change of Weierstrass coordinates, to $W$ itself, with the composite isogeny equal to multiplication by $N$; only the existence of the coordinate change is asserted. It is used for the invariance of the $j$-invariant under the double quotient and in the computation of places and widths on modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_variableChange_eq_fullKernelQuotient_fullKernelQuotient_comp_eq_smul.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_FullKernelQuotient
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_VariableChangePointEquiv

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
